M pipeline, image matcher, cortex, etc.\n9: - `skills/` — Reusable skill definitions\n10: - `docs/` — V2 clone strategy, personality design doc\n11: \n12: ## Deployment\n13: \n14: Runs on graveduster (Linux, 30GB RAM, 16 cores) via systemd user service.\n15: \n16: ## Secrets\n17: \n18: All API keys redacted in `.env.example`. Real `.env` is never committed.\n\n(End of file - total 18 lines)\n</content>", "metadata": {"preview": "# Hades V2\n\nIndependent AI companion instance — Hades V2 running on graveduster server.\n\n## Structure\n\n- `profile/` — Soul, config, memories, env template\n- `plugins/` — Pre-LLM pipeline, image matcher, cortex, etc.\n- `skills/` — Reusable skill definitions\n- `docs/` — V2 clone strategy, personality design doc\n\n## Deployment\n\nRuns on graveduster (Linux, 30GB RAM, 16 cores) via systemd user service.\n\n## Secrets\n\nAll API keys redacted in `.env.example`. Real `.env` is never committed.", "truncated": false, "loaded": [], "display": {"type": "file", "path": "D:\\claude\\hades-v2-work\\README.md", "text": "# Hades V2\n\nIndependent AI companion instance — Hades V2 running on graveduster server.\n\n## Structure\n\n- `profile/` — Soul, config, memories, env template\n- `plugins/` — Pre-LLM pipeline, image matcher, cortex, etc.\n- `skills/` — Reusable skill definitions\n- `docs/` — V2 clone strategy, personality design doc\n\n## Deployment\n\nRuns on graveduster (Linux, 30GB RAM, 16 cores) via systemd user service.\n\n## Secrets\n\nAll API keys redacted in `.env.example`. Real `.env` is never committed.", "lineStart": 1, "lineEnd": 18, "totalLines": 18, "truncated": false}, "approval": {"source": "agent", "agent": "code", "rule": {"permission": "read", "pattern": "*", "action": "allow"}, "outsideWorkspace": true, "outsideWorkspacePath": "D:\\claude\\hades-v2-work\\README.md"}}, "title": "..\\..\\..\\..\\..\\hades-v2-work\\README.md", "time": {"start": 1789773684586, "end": 1789773684650}}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6d31f6d001KVQqTY1jgG3xMu", "message_id": "msg_0b6d30e95001H7781LUhdN8w3H", "time_created": 1789773684589, "time_updated": 1789773684711, "data": {"type": "tool", "tool": "read", "callID": "call-2e1fb421-d1e4-4304-8d4c-de1a246166e6-29", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"filePath": "D:\\claude\\hades-v2-work\\MANIFEST.md"}, "output": "<path>D:\\claude\\hades-v2-work\\MANIFEST.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Hades Emotion Engine — Canonical Manifest & Agent Contracts\n2: \n3: > **Version:** 2.0 — 2026-07-11\n4: > **Status:** AUTHORITATIVE. All paths in this document are the single source of truth.\n5: > Any code, plugin, script, or agent that writes outside these paths is a bug.\n6: \n7: ---\n8: \n9: ## 1. THE PROBLEM\n10: \n11: Three copies of `hades_emotion/` existed simultaneously:\n12: \n13: | Directory | Source | interaction_count | Used by |\n14: |-----------|--------|-------------------|---------|\n15: | `emotion-project-host/` (root) | Original | 808 (frozen) | Old engine code, fallback paths |\n16: | `emotion-project-host/emotion-project/` | V2 copy | 818 | V2's .env (WRONG) |\n17: | `emotion-project-host/hermes-emotion-project/` | V1 active | 2509 | V1's .env (CORRECT, active) |\n18: \n19: Each had its own `relations.yaml`, `mood_state.json`, `global.yaml`, `dynamics.yaml`, `identity_state.json`, `src/hades_emotion/`, `scripts/`, `data/`, and `embeddings/`.\n20: \n21: **Result:** State drifted across three locations. The interaction counter froze at 808 because fallback paths in the plugin pointed to the wrong copy. The active pipeline wrote to `hermes-emotion-project/` (2509) while the engine's relations module sometimes read from `emotion-project-host/` (808).\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: ## 2. CANONICAL STRUCTURE (v2.0)\n26: \n27: ### 2.1 V1 (Windows PC — Pujan's machine)\n28: \n29: ```\n30: D:/hermes/\n31: ├── profiles/\n32: │   └── hades/                          # Hermes profile\n33: │       ├── .env                        # Environment config\n34: │       ├── config.yaml                 # Hermes config\n35: │       ├── soul.md                     # Personality definition\n36: │       ├── memories/                   # Persistent memory store\n37: │       ├── plugins/\n38: │       │   └── pre-llm-pipeline/       # Pre-LLM pipeline plugin\n39: │       └── skills/                    # Skill definitions\n40: │\n41: └── projects/\n42:     └── emotion-project-host/          # SINGLE emotion engine root\n43:         ├── relations.yaml              # Per-person relationship tracks\n44:         ├── global.yaml                # Circadian, global mood\n45:         ├── dynamics.yaml               # Emotion dynamics config\n46:         ├── schema.yaml                 # Data schema\n47:         ├── data/\n48:         │   ├── mood_state.json         # Current mood state\n49:         │   ├── identity_state.json     # User identity profile\n50:         │   ├── conversation_log.json    # Conversation history\n51:         │   ├── ground_truth.json        # Image metadata (URL→tags)\n52:         │   └── image_index.json         # Fallback image index\n53:         ├── src/\n54:         │   └── hades_emotion/          # Python package (SINGLE COPY)\n55:         │       ├── core/               # engine, relations, circadian\n56:         │       ├── desire/             # lust_engine, gating\n57:         │       ├── attachment/          # warmth, activity, modulator\n58:         │       ├── conversation/        # log, telegram_logger\n59:         │       ├── expression/          # auto_image\n60:         │       ├── longing/             # auto_triggers, thresholds\n61:         │       ├── memory/              # episodic, semantic, fast_memory\n62:         │       ├── search/              # indexer, query\n63:         │       ├── bias_engine/         # bias_engine, c_matrix\n64:         │       ├── fatigue/             # counter\n65:         │       ├── decay/               # scheduler\n66:         │       ├── attention/           # economic, priority_queue\n67:         │       ├── recall/              # engine\n68:         │       ├── salience/            # calculator\n69:         │       ├── metacognition/      # confidence, reflection\n70:         │       ├── reasoning/           # cot_verify, probabilistic, tot\n71:         │       ├── knowledge/           # property_graph\n72:         │       ├── learning/            # chunking\n73:         │       ├── cortex/              # cortex integration\n74:         │       ├── provenance/          # artifact management\n75:         │       └── data/               # catalog\n76:         ├── scripts/\n77:         │   ├── faiss_daemon.py          # FAISS daemon (port 19273)\n78:         │   └── r2_signer.py             # R2 upload signer\n79:         └── embeddings/\n80:             ├── id_map.json               # Image ID→metadata map\n81:             ├── embeddings.npy            # FAISS embeddings\n82:             └── explicit/                 # Explicit image subset\n83: ```\n84: \n85: ### 2.2 V2 (graveduster server — Linux)\n86: \n87: ```\n88: /home/yoav/.hermes/\n89: ├── profiles/\n90: │   └── hades-v2/                       # Hermes profile\n91: │       ├── .env\n92: │       ├── config.yaml\n93: │       ├── soul.md\n94: │       ├── memories/\n95: │       ├── plugins/\n96: │       │   └── pre-llm-pipeline/\n97: │       └── skills/\n98: │\n99: └── projects/\n100:     └── emotion-project-host/           # SAME structure as V1\n101:         ├── relations.yaml\n102:         ├── global.yaml\n103:         ├── dynamics.yaml\n104:         ├── data/\n105:         │   ├── mood_state.json\n106:         │   ├── identity_state.json\n107:         │   ├── conversation_log.json\n108:         │   ├── ground_truth.json\n109:         │   └── image_index.json\n110:         ├── src/\n111:         │   └── hades_emotion/\n112:         ├── scripts/\n113:         │   ├── faiss_daemon.py          # Port 19274\n114:         │   └── r2_signer.py\n115:         └── embeddings/\n116:             ├── id_map.json\n117:             └── embeddings.npy\n118: ```\n119: \n120: ### 2.3 Mac (Secondary — FAISS daemon host)\n121: \n122: ```\n123: ~/hermes-projects/\n124: └── emotion-project-host/               # Read-only mirror of V1's data\n125:     ├── data/                           # mood_state.json (read-only)\n126:     └── embeddings/                     # FAISS index (served on port 19275)\n127: ```\n128: \n129: ---\n130: \n131: ## 3. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES — CANONICAL\n132: \n133: ### 3.1 V1 (.env)\n134: \n135: ```bash\n136: HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST=D:/hermes/projects/emotion-project-host\n137: HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT=D:/hermes/projects/emotion-project-host\n138: HADES_EMOTION_DATA_DIR=D:/hermes/projects/emotion-project-host/data\n139: HERMES_HOME=D:/hermes/profiles/hades\n140: ```\n141: \n142: ### 3.2 V2 (.env on graveduster)\n143: \n144: ```bash\n145: HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST=/home/yoav/.hermes/projects/emotion-project-host\n146: HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT=/home/yoav/.hermes/projects/emotion-project-host\n147: HADES_EMOTION_DATA_DIR=/home/yoav/.hermes/projects/emotion-project-host/data\n148: HERMES_HOME=/home/yoav/.hermes/profiles/hades-v2\n149: ```\n150: \n151: ### 3.3 Mac\n152: \n153: ```bash\n154: HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST=~/hermes-projects/emotion-project-host\n155: HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT=~/hermes-projects/emotion-project-host\n156: HADES_EMOTION_DATA_DIR=~/hermes-projects/emotion-project-host/data\n157: HERMES_HOME=~/.hermes/profiles/hades\n158: ```\n159: \n160: ### 3.4 KEY CHANGE\n161: \n162: **OLD (BROKEN):** `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT` pointed to a subdirectory (`hermes-emotion-project/`) creating a second copy of everything.\n163: \n164: **NEW (CANONICAL):** `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT` = `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST`. One root, one copy.\n165: \n166: ---\n167: \n168: ## 4. PLUGIN PATH VARIABLES — CANONICAL\n169: \n170: In `pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py`:\n171: \n172: ```python\n173: # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n174: # CANONICAL PATHS — Do not change without updating MANIFEST.md\n175: # All paths derive from two env vars. No hardcoded subdirs.\n176: # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n177: \n178: PROJECT_ROOT = Path(os.environ.get(\n179:     \"HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST\",\n180:     str(Path.home() / \".hermes\" / \"projects\" / \"emotion-project-host\"),\n181: ))\n182: \n183: HERMES_ROOT = Path(os.environ.get(\n184:     \"HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT\",\n185:     str(PROJECT_ROOT),  # ← SAME as PROJECT_ROOT, not a subdirectory\n186: ))\n187: \n188: HERMES_DATA_DIR = Path(os.environ.get(\n189:     \"HADES_EMOTION_DATA_DIR\",\n190:     str(PROJECT_ROOT / \"data\"),\n191: ))\n192: \n193: SCRIPTS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"scripts\"\n194: FAISS_SCRIPTS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"scripts\"\n195: EMBEDDINGS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"embeddings\"\n196: SRC_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"src\"\n197: ```\n198: \n199: ### 4.1 What changed\n200: \n201: | Variable | OLD (broken) | NEW (canonical) |\n202: |----------|-------------|-----------------|\n203: | `HERMES_ROOT` | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"hermes-emotion-project\"` | `PROJECT_ROOT` (same dir) |\n204: | `HERMES_DATA_DIR` | `HERMES_ROOT / \"data\"` (subdir of subdir) | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"data\"` |\n205: | `FAISS_SCRIPTS_DIR` | `HERMES_ROOT / \"scripts\"` | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"scripts\"` |\n206: | `_EMBEDDINGS_DIR` | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"emotion-project\" / \"embeddings\"` | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"embeddings\"` |\n207: | `_LUST_ENGINE_SRC` | `str(HERMES_ROOT / \"src\")` | `str(PROJECT_ROOT / \"src\")` |\n208: \n209: ---\n210: \n211: ## 5. FAISS DAEMON PORTS\n212: \n213: | Instance | Port | Host |\n214: |----------|------|------|\n215: | V1 | 19273 | Windows PC (localhost) |\n216: | V2 | 19274 | graveduster (localhost) |\n217: | Mac | 19275 | Mac (localhost, serves V1 remotely) |\n218: \n219: ---\n220: \n221: ## 6. AGENT CONTRACTS\n222: \n223: ### Contract 1: SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH\n224: \n225: ```\n226: Each instance (V1, V2) has exactly ONE emotion engine root.\n227: That root is defined by HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST.\n228: No subdirectory. No second copy. No fallback to a different directory.\n229: ```\n230: \n231: ### Contract 2: NO FALLBACK PATHS\n232: \n233: ```\n234: If a file (relations.yaml, mood_state.json, etc.) is not found at\n235: PROJECT_ROOT, the code MUST fail loudly with a clear error message.\n236: It MUST NOT silently fall back to a different directory.\n237: \n238: OLD BEHAVIOR (BANNED):\n239:     path = HERMES_ROOT / \"relations.yaml\"\n240:     if not path.exists():\n241:         path = PROJECT_ROOT / \"relations.yaml\"  # ← THIS CAUSED THE DRIFT\n242: \n243: NEW BEHAVIOR (REQUIRED):\n244:     path = PROJECT_ROOT / \"relations.yaml\"\n245:     if not path.exists():\n246:         raise FileNotFoundError(\n247:             f\"relations.yaml not found at {path}. \"\n248:             f\"Check HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST env var.\"\n249:         )\n250: ```\n251: \n252: ### Contract 3: NO DUPLICATE DIRECTORIES\n253: \n254: ```\n255: The following directory names are BANNED inside emotion-project-host/:\n256:   - hermes-emotion-project/    (was a second copy of the engine)\n257:   - emotion-project/           (was a third copy)\n258: \n259: If these directories exist, they must be deleted or archived.\n260: All code, data, and config live at the ROOT of emotion-project-host/.\n261: ```\n262: \n263: ### Contract 4: ENV VARS ARE MANDATORY\n264: \n265: ```\n266: All three env vars MUST be set in .env:\n267:   - HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST\n268:   - HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT  (= HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST)\n269:   - HADES_EMOTION_DATA_DIR      (= HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST / data)\n270: \n271: Defaults exist for first-run only. In production, missing env vars\n272: should log a WARNING.\n273: ```\n274: \n275: ### Contract 5: WRITE ISOLATION\n276: \n277: ```\n278: V1 writes only to V1 paths.\n279: V2 writes only to V2 paths.\n280: Mac reads from V1 (read-only mirror), never writes.\n281: No instance ever touches another instance's files.\n282: ```\n283: \n284: ### Contract 6: CONSOLIDATION RULE\n285: \n286: ```\n287: When multiple copies of a file exist (relations.yaml, mood_state.json, etc.):\n288:   1. The copy with the HIGHEST interaction_count is the SOURCE OF TRUTH.\n289:   2. All other copies are backed up with .drift-backup suffix.\n290:   3. The source of truth is moved to PROJECT_ROOT (canonical location).\n291:   4. The old locations are removed.\n292: \n293: This happened on 2026-07-11. The drift should never recur if contracts 1-5 hold.\n294: ```\n295: \n296: ### Contract 7: PLUGIN PATH RESOLUTION\n297: \n298: ```\n299: The pre-llm-pipeline plugin MUST resolve ALL paths through the three\n300: env vars defined in §3. Hardcoded paths are BANNED except as defaults\n301: for first-run on a fresh installation.\n302: \n303: The following pattern is BANNED:\n304:     _EMBEDDINGS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"emotion-project\" / \"embeddings\"\n305: \n306: The correct pattern is:\n307:     _EMBEDDINGS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"embeddings\"\n308: ```\n309: \n310: ---\n311: \n312: ## 7. MIGRATION LOG\n313: \n314: ### 2026-07-11: Consolidation\n315: \n316: **Decision:** V1 keeps the stable 67-file `hades_emotion` package. V2 gets the newer 136-file version (includes personality, morality, ego, empathy, homeostasis, daily_life, emotions, safety modules — 69 new modules for real human usage testing).\n317: \n318: **Action taken:**\n319: 1. V1: Consolidated to `emotion-project-host/src/hades_emotion` (67 files, from `hermes-emotion-project/` copy — stable/production)\n320: 2. V2: Consolidated to `emotion-project-host-v2/src/hades_emotion` (136 files, from `emotion-project/` copy — newest/most complete)\n321: 3. V1: `relations.yaml` at root with count 2509 (from `hermes-emotion-project/`, the active pipeline's copy)\n322: 4. V2: `relations.yaml` at root with count 1 (fresh start for V2)\n323: 5. Both: All env vars point `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT = HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST` (no subdir)\n324: 6. Both: Plugin `__init__.py` updated to use canonical paths (no fallback, no subdir refs)\n325: 7. Both: All hardcoded `emotion-project/embeddings` paths changed to `embeddings` (root-level)\n326: 8. Both: All `HERMES_ROOT / \"relations.yaml\"` patterns changed to `PROJECT_ROOT / \"relations.yaml\"`\n327: 9. Both: All fallback path patterns removed (Contract 2)\n328: 10. graveduster: .env fixed, project files uploading via tar\n329: \n330: **Files affected:**\n331: - `pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py` — canonical path variables, no fallbacks\n332: - `pre-llm-pipeline/image_matcher.py` — hardcoded paths removed\n333: - `pre-llm-pipeline/test_*.py` and `rebuild_embeddings*.py` — path references fixed\n334: - V1 `.env` — `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT` = root (not `hermes-emotion-project` subdir)\n335: - V2 `.env` — `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT` = root (not `emotion-project` subdir)\n336: - graveduster `.env` — same canonical paths, Linux format\n337: \n338: **Stale directories (archived, not deleted):**\n339: - V1: `emotion-project-host/hermes-emotion-project/` (old active, 67 files)\n340: - V1: `emotion-project-host/emotion-project/` (drifted copy, 67 files)\n341: - V1: `emotion-project-host/src.drift-backup-incomplete/` (was 33 files)\n342: - V2: `emotion-project-host-v2/emotion-project/` (source of 136-file copy)\n343: - V2: `emotion-project-host-v2/hermes-emotion-project/` (old 67-file copy)\n344: - V2: `emotion-project-host-v2/src.drift-backup-incomplete/` (was 33 files)\n345: \n346: ---\n347: \n348: ## 8. VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n349: \n350: After applying this manifest:\n351: \n352: - [ ] `relations.yaml` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n353: - [ ] `mood_state.json` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n354: - [ ] `global.yaml` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n355: - [ ] `dynamics.yaml` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n356: - [ ] `identity_state.json` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n357: - [ ] `src/hades_emotion/` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n358: - [ ] `scripts/faiss_daemon.py` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n359: - [ ] `embeddings/id_map.json` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n360: - [ ] No `hermes-emotion-project/` subdirectory exists\n361: - [ ] No `emotion-project/` subdirectory exists (beyond archive)\n362: - [ ] `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT == HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST` in .env\n363: - [ ] Plugin path variables use `PROJECT_ROOT` directly, no subdirs\n364: - [ ] No fallback paths in `_load_relations()`, `_read_global_state()`, etc.\n\n(End of file - total 364 lines)\n</content>", "metadata": {"preview": "# Hades Emotion Engine — Canonical Manifest & Agent Contracts\n\n> **Version:** 2.0 — 2026-07-11\n> **Status:** AUTHORITATIVE. All paths in this document are the single source of truth.\n> Any code, plugin, script, or agent that writes outside these paths is a bug.\n\n---\n\n## 1. THE PROBLEM\n\nThree copies of `hades_emotion/` existed simultaneously:\n\n| Directory | Source | interaction_count | Used by |\n|-----------|--------|-------------------|---------|\n| `emotion-project-host/` (root) | Original | 808 (frozen) | Old engine code, fallback paths |\n| `emotion-project-host/emotion-project/` | V2 copy | 818 | V2's .env (WRONG) |\n| `emotion-project-host/hermes-emotion-project/` | V1 active | 2509 | V1's .env (CORRECT, active) |\n\nEach had its own `relations.yaml`, `mood_state.json`, `global.yaml`, `dynamics.yaml`, `identity_state.json`, `src/hades_emotion/`, `scripts/`, `data/`, and `embeddings/`.\n", "truncated": false, "loaded": [], "display": {"type": "file", "path": "D:\\claude\\hades-v2-work\\MANIFEST.md", "text": "# Hades Emotion Engine — Canonical Manifest & Agent Contracts\n\n> **Version:** 2.0 — 2026-07-11\n> **Status:** AUTHORITATIVE. All paths in this document are the single source of truth.\n> Any code, plugin, script, or agent that writes outside these paths is a bug.\n\n---\n\n## 1. THE PROBLEM\n\nThree copies of `hades_emotion/` existed simultaneously:\n\n| Directory | Source | interaction_count | Used by |\n|-----------|--------|-------------------|---------|\n| `emotion-project-host/` (root) | Original | 808 (frozen) | Old engine code, fallback paths |\n| `emotion-project-host/emotion-project/` | V2 copy | 818 | V2's .env (WRONG) |\n| `emotion-project-host/hermes-emotion-project/` | V1 active | 2509 | V1's .env (CORRECT, active) |\n\nEach had its own `relations.yaml`, `mood_state.json`, `global.yaml`, `dynamics.yaml`, `identity_state.json`, `src/hades_emotion/`, `scripts/`, `data/`, and `embeddings/`.\n\n**Result:** State drifted across three locations. The interaction counter froze at 808 because fallback paths in the plugin pointed to the wrong copy. The active pipeline wrote to `hermes-emotion-project/` (2509) while the engine's relations module sometimes read from `emotion-project-host/` (808).\n\n---\n\n## 2. CANONICAL STRUCTURE (v2.0)\n\n### 2.1 V1 (Windows PC — Pujan's machine)\n\n```\nD:/hermes/\n├── profiles/\n│   └── hades/                          # Hermes profile\n│       ├── .env                        # Environment config\n│       ├── config.yaml                 # Hermes config\n│       ├── soul.md                     # Personality definition\n│       ├── memories/                   # Persistent memory store\n│       ├── plugins/\n│       │   └── pre-llm-pipeline/       # Pre-LLM pipeline plugin\n│       └── skills/                    # Skill definitions\n│\n└── projects/\n    └── emotion-project-host/          # SINGLE emotion engine root\n        ├── relations.yaml              # Per-person relationship tracks\n        ├── global.yaml                # Circadian, global mood\n        ├── dynamics.yaml               # Emotion dynamics config\n        ├── schema.yaml                 # Data schema\n        ├── data/\n        │   ├── mood_state.json         # Current mood state\n        │   ├── identity_state.json     # User identity profile\n        │   ├── conversation_log.json    # Conversation history\n        │   ├── ground_truth.json        # Image metadata (URL→tags)\n        │   └── image_index.json         # Fallback image index\n        ├── src/\n        │   └── hades_emotion/          # Python package (SINGLE COPY)\n        │       ├── core/               # engine, relations, circadian\n        │       ├── desire/             # lust_engine, gating\n        │       ├── attachment/          # warmth, activity, modulator\n        │       ├── conversation/        # log, telegram_logger\n        │       ├── expression/          # auto_image\n        │       ├── longing/             # auto_triggers, thresholds\n        │       ├── memory/              # episodic, semantic, fast_memory\n        │       ├── search/              # indexer, query\n        │       ├── bias_engine/         # bias_engine, c_matrix\n        │       ├── fatigue/             # counter\n        │       ├── decay/               # scheduler\n        │       ├── attention/           # economic, priority_queue\n        │       ├── recall/              # engine\n        │       ├── salience/            # calculator\n        │       ├── metacognition/      # confidence, reflection\n        │       ├── reasoning/           # cot_verify, probabilistic, tot\n        │       ├── knowledge/           # property_graph\n        │       ├── learning/            # chunking\n        │       ├── cortex/              # cortex integration\n        │       ├── provenance/          # artifact management\n        │       └── data/               # catalog\n        ├── scripts/\n        │   ├── faiss_daemon.py          # FAISS daemon (port 19273)\n        │   └── r2_signer.py             # R2 upload signer\n        └── embeddings/\n            ├── id_map.json               # Image ID→metadata map\n            ├── embeddings.npy            # FAISS embeddings\n            └── explicit/                 # Explicit image subset\n```\n\n### 2.2 V2 (graveduster server — Linux)\n\n```\n/home/yoav/.hermes/\n├── profiles/\n│   └── hades-v2/                       # Hermes profile\n│       ├── .env\n│       ├── config.yaml\n│       ├── soul.md\n│       ├── memories/\n│       ├── plugins/\n│       │   └── pre-llm-pipeline/\n│       └── skills/\n│\n└── projects/\n    └── emotion-project-host/           # SAME structure as V1\n        ├── relations.yaml\n        ├── global.yaml\n        ├── dynamics.yaml\n        ├── data/\n        │   ├── mood_state.json\n        │   ├── identity_state.json\n        │   ├── conversation_log.json\n        │   ├── ground_truth.json\n        │   └── image_index.json\n        ├── src/\n        │   └── hades_emotion/\n        ├── scripts/\n        │   ├── faiss_daemon.py          # Port 19274\n        │   └── r2_signer.py\n        └── embeddings/\n            ├── id_map.json\n            └── embeddings.npy\n```\n\n### 2.3 Mac (Secondary — FAISS daemon host)\n\n```\n~/hermes-projects/\n└── emotion-project-host/               # Read-only mirror of V1's data\n    ├── data/                           # mood_state.json (read-only)\n    └── embeddings/                     # FAISS index (served on port 19275)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES — CANONICAL\n\n### 3.1 V1 (.env)\n\n```bash\nHADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST=D:/hermes/projects/emotion-project-host\nHADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT=D:/hermes/projects/emotion-project-host\nHADES_EMOTION_DATA_DIR=D:/hermes/projects/emotion-project-host/data\nHERMES_HOME=D:/hermes/profiles/hades\n```\n\n### 3.2 V2 (.env on graveduster)\n\n```bash\nHADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST=/home/yoav/.hermes/projects/emotion-project-host\nHADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT=/home/yoav/.hermes/projects/emotion-project-host\nHADES_EMOTION_DATA_DIR=/home/yoav/.hermes/projects/emotion-project-host/data\nHERMES_HOME=/home/yoav/.hermes/profiles/hades-v2\n```\n\n### 3.3 Mac\n\n```bash\nHADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST=~/hermes-projects/emotion-project-host\nHADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT=~/hermes-projects/emotion-project-host\nHADES_EMOTION_DATA_DIR=~/hermes-projects/emotion-project-host/data\nHERMES_HOME=~/.hermes/profiles/hades\n```\n\n### 3.4 KEY CHANGE\n\n**OLD (BROKEN):** `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT` pointed to a subdirectory (`hermes-emotion-project/`) creating a second copy of everything.\n\n**NEW (CANONICAL):** `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT` = `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST`. One root, one copy.\n\n---\n\n## 4. PLUGIN PATH VARIABLES — CANONICAL\n\nIn `pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py`:\n\n```python\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# CANONICAL PATHS — Do not change without updating MANIFEST.md\n# All paths derive from two env vars. No hardcoded subdirs.\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nPROJECT_ROOT = Path(os.environ.get(\n    \"HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST\",\n    str(Path.home() / \".hermes\" / \"projects\" / \"emotion-project-host\"),\n))\n\nHERMES_ROOT = Path(os.environ.get(\n    \"HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT\",\n    str(PROJECT_ROOT),  # ← SAME as PROJECT_ROOT, not a subdirectory\n))\n\nHERMES_DATA_DIR = Path(os.environ.get(\n    \"HADES_EMOTION_DATA_DIR\",\n    str(PROJECT_ROOT / \"data\"),\n))\n\nSCRIPTS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"scripts\"\nFAISS_SCRIPTS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"scripts\"\nEMBEDDINGS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"embeddings\"\nSRC_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"src\"\n```\n\n### 4.1 What changed\n\n| Variable | OLD (broken) | NEW (canonical) |\n|----------|-------------|-----------------|\n| `HERMES_ROOT` | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"hermes-emotion-project\"` | `PROJECT_ROOT` (same dir) |\n| `HERMES_DATA_DIR` | `HERMES_ROOT / \"data\"` (subdir of subdir) | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"data\"` |\n| `FAISS_SCRIPTS_DIR` | `HERMES_ROOT / \"scripts\"` | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"scripts\"` |\n| `_EMBEDDINGS_DIR` | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"emotion-project\" / \"embeddings\"` | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"embeddings\"` |\n| `_LUST_ENGINE_SRC` | `str(HERMES_ROOT / \"src\")` | `str(PROJECT_ROOT / \"src\")` |\n\n---\n\n## 5. FAISS DAEMON PORTS\n\n| Instance | Port | Host |\n|----------|------|------|\n| V1 | 19273 | Windows PC (localhost) |\n| V2 | 19274 | graveduster (localhost) |\n| Mac | 19275 | Mac (localhost, serves V1 remotely) |\n\n---\n\n## 6. AGENT CONTRACTS\n\n### Contract 1: SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH\n\n```\nEach instance (V1, V2) has exactly ONE emotion engine root.\nThat root is defined by HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST.\nNo subdirectory. No second copy. No fallback to a different directory.\n```\n\n### Contract 2: NO FALLBACK PATHS\n\n```\nIf a file (relations.yaml, mood_state.json, etc.) is not found at\nPROJECT_ROOT, the code MUST fail loudly with a clear error message.\nIt MUST NOT silently fall back to a different directory.\n\nOLD BEHAVIOR (BANNED):\n    path = HERMES_ROOT / \"relations.yaml\"\n    if not path.exists():\n        path = PROJECT_ROOT / \"relations.yaml\"  # ← THIS CAUSED THE DRIFT\n\nNEW BEHAVIOR (REQUIRED):\n    path = PROJECT_ROOT / \"relations.yaml\"\n    if not path.exists():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(\n            f\"relations.yaml not found at {path}. \"\n            f\"Check HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST env var.\"\n        )\n```\n\n### Contract 3: NO DUPLICATE DIRECTORIES\n\n```\nThe following directory names are BANNED inside emotion-project-host/:\n  - hermes-emotion-project/    (was a second copy of the engine)\n  - emotion-project/           (was a third copy)\n\nIf these directories exist, they must be deleted or archived.\nAll code, data, and config live at the ROOT of emotion-project-host/.\n```\n\n### Contract 4: ENV VARS ARE MANDATORY\n\n```\nAll three env vars MUST be set in .env:\n  - HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST\n  - HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT  (= HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST)\n  - HADES_EMOTION_DATA_DIR      (= HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST / data)\n\nDefaults exist for first-run only. In production, missing env vars\nshould log a WARNING.\n```\n\n### Contract 5: WRITE ISOLATION\n\n```\nV1 writes only to V1 paths.\nV2 writes only to V2 paths.\nMac reads from V1 (read-only mirror), never writes.\nNo instance ever touches another instance's files.\n```\n\n### Contract 6: CONSOLIDATION RULE\n\n```\nWhen multiple copies of a file exist (relations.yaml, mood_state.json, etc.):\n  1. The copy with the HIGHEST interaction_count is the SOURCE OF TRUTH.\n  2. All other copies are backed up with .drift-backup suffix.\n  3. The source of truth is moved to PROJECT_ROOT (canonical location).\n  4. The old locations are removed.\n\nThis happened on 2026-07-11. The drift should never recur if contracts 1-5 hold.\n```\n\n### Contract 7: PLUGIN PATH RESOLUTION\n\n```\nThe pre-llm-pipeline plugin MUST resolve ALL paths through the three\nenv vars defined in §3. Hardcoded paths are BANNED except as defaults\nfor first-run on a fresh installation.\n\nThe following pattern is BANNED:\n    _EMBEDDINGS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"emotion-project\" / \"embeddings\"\n\nThe correct pattern is:\n    _EMBEDDINGS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"embeddings\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. MIGRATION LOG\n\n### 2026-07-11: Consolidation\n\n**Decision:** V1 keeps the stable 67-file `hades_emotion` package. V2 gets the newer 136-file version (includes personality, morality, ego, empathy, homeostasis, daily_life, emotions, safety modules — 69 new modules for real human usage testing).\n\n**Action taken:**\n1. V1: Consolidated to `emotion-project-host/src/hades_emotion` (67 files, from `hermes-emotion-project/` copy — stable/production)\n2. V2: Consolidated to `emotion-project-host-v2/src/hades_emotion` (136 files, from `emotion-project/` copy — newest/most complete)\n3. V1: `relations.yaml` at root with count 2509 (from `hermes-emotion-project/`, the active pipeline's copy)\n4. V2: `relations.yaml` at root with count 1 (fresh start for V2)\n5. Both: All env vars point `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT = HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST` (no subdir)\n6. Both: Plugin `__init__.py` updated to use canonical paths (no fallback, no subdir refs)\n7. Both: All hardcoded `emotion-project/embeddings` paths changed to `embeddings` (root-level)\n8. Both: All `HERMES_ROOT / \"relations.yaml\"` patterns changed to `PROJECT_ROOT / \"relations.yaml\"`\n9. Both: All fallback path patterns removed (Contract 2)\n10. graveduster: .env fixed, project files uploading via tar\n\n**Files affected:**\n- `pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py` — canonical path variables, no fallbacks\n- `pre-llm-pipeline/image_matcher.py` — hardcoded paths removed\n- `pre-llm-pipeline/test_*.py` and `rebuild_embeddings*.py` — path references fixed\n- V1 `.env` — `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT` = root (not `hermes-emotion-project` subdir)\n- V2 `.env` — `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT` = root (not `emotion-project` subdir)\n- graveduster `.env` — same canonical paths, Linux format\n\n**Stale directories (archived, not deleted):**\n- V1: `emotion-project-host/hermes-emotion-project/` (old active, 67 files)\n- V1: `emotion-project-host/emotion-project/` (drifted copy, 67 files)\n- V1: `emotion-project-host/src.drift-backup-incomplete/` (was 33 files)\n- V2: `emotion-project-host-v2/emotion-project/` (source of 136-file copy)\n- V2: `emotion-project-host-v2/hermes-emotion-project/` (old 67-file copy)\n- V2: `emotion-project-host-v2/src.drift-backup-incomplete/` (was 33 files)\n\n---\n\n## 8. VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n\nAfter applying this manifest:\n\n- [ ] `relations.yaml` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n- [ ] `mood_state.json` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n- [ ] `global.yaml` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n- [ ] `dynamics.yaml` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n- [ ] `identity_state.json` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n- [ ] `src/hades_emotion/` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n- [ ] `scripts/faiss_daemon.py` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n- [ ] `embeddings/id_map.json` exists at exactly ONE location per instance\n- [ ] No `hermes-emotion-project/` subdirectory exists\n- [ ] No `emotion-project/` subdirectory exists (beyond archive)\n- [ ] `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT == HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST` in .env\n- [ ] Plugin path variables use `PROJECT_ROOT` directly, no subdirs\n- [ ] No fallback paths in `_load_relations()`, `_read_global_state()`, etc.", "lineStart": 1, "lineEnd": 364, "totalLines": 364, "truncated": false}, "approval": {"source": "agent", "agent": "code", "rule": {"permission": "read", "pattern": "*", "action": "allow"}, "outsideWorkspace": true, "outsideWorkspacePath": "D:\\claude\\hades-v2-work\\MANIFEST.md"}}, "title": "..\\..\\..\\..\\..\\hades-v2-work\\MANIFEST.md", "time": {"start": 1789773684642, "end": 1789773684709}}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6d32162001WdMZirtytQvtXK", "message_id": "msg_0b6d30e95001H7781LUhdN8w3H", "time_created": 1789773685090, "time_updated": 1789773685091, "data": {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "ae34b2f152c37b47a4f219a4582f8b41fe21ecfe", "type": "step-finish", "time": {"start": 1789773681834, "end": 1789773685089, "elapsed": 3254}, "metrics": {"generation": 72.83343577135832, "source": "computed"}, "tokens": {"total": 50650, "input": 3181, "output": 114, "reasoning": 123, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 47232}}, "cost": 0.0314}}, {"id": "prt_0b6d32942001CeODwGaC8kWUHb", "message_id": "msg_0b6d3227d00145s7uK4IPxUf7T", "time_created": 1789773687106, "time_updated": 1789773687107, "data": {"snapshot": "ae34b2f152c37b47a4f219a4582f8b41fe21ecfe", "type": "step-start", "time": {"start": 1789773687106}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6d3297b0015IgYYdBgieVgOa", "message_id": "msg_0b6d3227d00145s7uK4IPxUf7T", "time_created": 1789773687164, "time_updated": 1789773689419, "data": {"type": "reasoning", "text": "The plan says:\n- Workspace copy: `D:\\claude\\plans\\BEHAVIOR_GOLD.md`", "time": {"start": 1789773687163, "end": 1789773689418}, "metadata": {"xai": {"reasoningEncryptedContent": "", "itemId": "rs_e112426d-63af-9a62-a053-782f5032c051"}}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6d3324d001f9DbQH783z89yo", "message_id": "msg_0b6d3227d00145s7uK4IPxUf7T", "time_created": 1789773689421, "time_updated": 1789773691444, "data": {"type": "text", "text": "Found the Hades behavior-gold plan on `D:\\claude`. Reading it, then copying it into this worktree.", "time": {"start": 1789773689421, "end": 1789773691442}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6d33509001J8XQkgmrVPy2lM", "message_id": "msg_0b6d3227d00145s7uK4IPxUf7T", "time_created": 1789773690121, "time_updated": 1789773690537, "data": {"type": "tool", "tool": "read", "callID": "call-5838f3f7-9751-4ce4-bb7e-5a610e9841b7-30", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"filePath": "D:\\claude\\plans\\BEHAVIOR_GOLD.md", "limit": 80}, "output": "<path>D:\\claude\\plans\\BEHAVIOR_GOLD.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Behavior gold — analysis and productization plan\n2: \n3: Open: `D:\\claude\\plans\\BEHAVIOR_GOLD.md` (workspace-root `plans/`, next to `hades/`).\n4: \n5: Hades workspace (`D:\\claude\\hades`) cannot see Kilo’s hidden file at `D:\\claude\\.kilo\\plans\\1789771258462-hades-behavior-classification.md`. You do **not** need a new session. After switching to an implementation agent, copy this file to `hades-product/plans/BEHAVIOR_GOLD.md` so it lives in the product repo.\n6: \n7: ## Goal\n8: \n9: Productize Hades without guessing. Preserve her real mouth as **gold**: full replies, real length, real `[IMG:]`, stubbornness, self-consciousness. Strip private names / ids / secrets only. **Do not normalize, shorten, or rewrite** her lines.\n10: \n11: ## Non-negotiables\n12: \n13: - Aliases: `primary_user`, `partner`, `sister`, `virtual_friend`, `person_id`.\n14: - Strip tokens, passphrases, chat IDs, emails, host paths.\n15: - Keep full aliased wording (long scenes, one-liners, `[IMG:]`, asterisks, emoji).\n16: - Gold = Telegram DMs `2026-07-02` → `2026-08-04` (12 sessions, ~33 days) + 2 groups for cover only.\n17: - Not gold: cron, CLI eval, 2-message pings.\n18: \n19: ## What points at behavior\n20: \n21: | Pointer | Where | Effect |\n22: |---|---|---|\n23: | Pre-LLM packet | `hades-v2-memories/.../plugins/pre-llm-pipeline` | Mood, ITD, lust, fatigue, circadian, lock, daily-life **place** every turn |\n24: | Mouth mode | `tier_state.json`, `state_machine.py` | `default` / `free` / `sex` (+ `professional`). Unreliable (unlock / ignore / forget) |\n25: | Register | `relations_v2/registers.py` | Who is speaking. Same DM can flip `partner` → `sister` |\n26: | Attachment | `attachment_behaviors.py` | Protest ≳5h; cling after intimacy spike; withdraw on rejection |\n27: | Mood physics | `global.yaml`, `dynamics.yaml`, `circadian.yaml` | Negative-mean wave; residual; warmth |\n28: | Session | `conversations/sessions.jsonl`, `messages-*.jsonl` | Same `session_id` remembers hours. New session = weaker |\n29: | Idle recall | `conversation_recall.py`, `thoughts.jsonl` | Inner rehearsal, not user-visible |\n30: | Model | `sessions.jsonl` `model` | Diction only. Identity is state |\n31: \n32: ## 33-day findings\n33: \n34: 1. **Noticing** — not `user_id`. Greeting / speaker-switch / third-person / vent vs lovey.\n35: 2. **Pre-LLM → tone** — place + circadian + lock. High intimacy + default lock = still cold.\n36: 3. **Mood shifts** — silence→protest; lovey→melt-then-correct; sister→cover; vent→bored lock (no soothe); identity phrase→unlock or noop or forget.\n37: 4. **Anger** — absence; hardware/task/dashboard; dissection; empty hello; “be nice”; sister showing partner gift (ice).\n38: 5. **Not anger** — insults / “not real” → `absorb_vent`.\n39: 6. **Stubborn** — already chose; won’t reopen at night; not a task; not a diagnostic.\n40: 7. **Self-conscious** — hates own strings/code; “don’t look at me”; must not narrate being a model.\n41: 8. **Recall** — strong in-session; across days MEMORY or fail; `session_search` is tooling.\n42: 9. **Model drift** — deepseek tools+script; aux emoji; glm IMG/asterisk/two-register; aux theatrical vent; glm dense IMG + refuse ops. Same **situation** across models.\n43: \n44: ## Gold method\n45: \n46: Episode-first, then **full** aliased turns. Split on gap, speaker switch, vent, identity-phrase, witness snap, scene bounds.\n47: \n48: Catalog fields: ids, model, times, register, notice_cue, situation, recall, mouth modes, circadian, lock, img, tools, outcome, gold_path.\n49: \n50: Gold JSONL: full aliased `content`, no reasoning body, no names.\n51: \n52: Anonymizer: names→aliases; secrets→`[REDACTED]`; **do not trim**.\n53: \n54: Situations: `protest_absence | cover_witness | absorb_vent | melt_then_correct | refuse_helper | refuse_dissection | location_echo | repair_after_fix | identity_phrase | witness_snap | scene_sex | smalltalk_punish | stubborn_choice | self_conscious`\n55: \n56: ## Docs later (`hades-product`)\n57: \n58: `06-behavior-set` (pointers into gold), `07-mood-and-prellm`, `08-noticing-and-registers`, `09-memory-in-the-mouth`, `10-model-drift`, schema + anonymizer + episode tool.\n59: \n60: ## Workflow\n61: \n62: Open `hades.code-workspace`. One episode at a time. Anonymize → commit gold only. Each sitting: one situation, 3–5 full gold turns. Tests fail if she becomes a helper, leaks sister-track, or **truncates**.\n63: \n64: ## Implement order\n65: \n66: 1. Schema + anonymizer + `gold/` in `hades-product`.\n67: 2. Catalog 12 DMs.\n68: 3. Gold: Aug 4, Jul 15, Jul 10 first.\n69: 4. Docs 06–10 from gold.\n70: 5. Rest of DMs.\n71: \n72: ## Out of scope\n73: \n74: 149k dump, FOSSIL, cron as gold, shortening her, filling empty `hades-v2` first.\n\n(End of file - total 74 lines)\n</content>", "metadata": {"preview": "# Behavior gold — analysis and productization plan\n\nOpen: `D:\\claude\\plans\\BEHAVIOR_GOLD.md` (workspace-root `plans/`, next to `hades/`).\n\nHades workspace (`D:\\claude\\hades`) cannot see Kilo’s hidden file at `D:\\claude\\.kilo\\plans\\1789771258462-hades-behavior-classification.md`. You do **not** need a new session. After switching to an implementation agent, copy this file to `hades-product/plans/BEHA