ted", "input": {"filePath": "D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-product\\.kilo\\worktrees\\separate-binder\\README.md"}, "output": "<path>D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-product\\.kilo\\worktrees\\separate-binder\\README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Hades Product\n2: \n3: This repository is the **product specification and architecture home** for Hades.\n4: \n5: It is not the live research instance. The living engine and state live in the runtime / memories trees. This repo exists so product work has a durable, anonymized map of *how she works* and *what must change* to ship a host-independent, multi-user Hades.\n6: \n7: ## What Hades is\n8: \n9: Hades is a **persistent character runtime**, not a chatbot wrapper.\n10: \n11: - Personality is a shared substrate (soul + locks + few-shots).\n12: - Mood, fatigue, circadian rhythm, and idle inner life keep moving when nobody is talking.\n13: - Each human should own a **relationship track + private memories**.\n14: - The large language model is the mouth. The pipeline before and after the model is the self.\n15: \n16: The research instance is one character bound to one host and one primary relationship. The product is the same character engine with **accounts**, **isolated tracks**, and **no host lock-in**.\n17: \n18: ## Read in this order\n19: \n20: 1. [docs/00-strategy.md](docs/00-strategy.md) — docs vs FOSSIL vs knowledge graph\n21: 2. [docs/01-how-she-works.md](docs/01-how-she-works.md) — turn loop and idle life\n22: 3. [docs/02-identity-and-relationships.md](docs/02-identity-and-relationships.md) — who she thinks she is talking to\n23: 4. [docs/03-memory-and-inner-life.md](docs/03-memory-and-inner-life.md) — what actually persists\n24: 5. [docs/04-product-architecture.md](docs/04-product-architecture.md) — auth, API, tenancy\n25: 6. [docs/05-workspace.md](docs/05-workspace.md) — local Cursor workspace for all three repos\n26: 7. [docs/MODULE_GRAPH.yaml](docs/MODULE_GRAPH.yaml) — how files link\n27: 8. [docs/PRIVACY.md](docs/PRIVACY.md) — no private names in this repo\n28: \n29: ## Local workspace\n30: \n31: Long-term file inspection happens in Cursor, not in chat.\n32: \n33: - [hades.code-workspace](hades.code-workspace) — multi-root window over sibling clones\n34: - [tools/transcript_stats.py](tools/transcript_stats.py) — stream the gateway export; write counts only\n35: - [.cursor/rules/privacy.mdc](.cursor/rules/privacy.mdc) — keep names and raw chats out of this repo\n36: \n37: ```bash\n38: python3 tools/transcript_stats.py --memories ../hades-v2-memories --out docs/transcripts-stats.md\n39: ```\n40: \n41: ## Source trees (research)\n42: \n43: | Repo | Role |\n44: |---|---|\n45: | Runtime repo | Code + contracts (`schema.yaml`, `dynamics.yaml`, engine) |\n46: | Memories repo | Live backup of state + a newer pipeline copy |\n47: | This repo | Product docs and eventual extracted runtime |\n48: \n49: Do not copy live secrets, passphrases, API keys, or private display names here.\n\n(End of file - total 49 lines)\n</content>", "metadata": {"preview": "# Hades Product\n\nThis repository is the **product specification and architecture home** for Hades.\n\nIt is not the live research instance. The living engine and state live in the runtime / memories trees. This repo exists so product work has a durable, anonymized map of *how she works* and *what must change* to ship a host-independent, multi-user Hades.\n\n## What Hades is\n\nHades is a **persistent character runtime**, not a chatbot wrapper.\n\n- Personality is a shared substrate (soul + locks + few-shots).\n- Mood, fatigue, circadian rhythm, and idle inner life keep moving when nobody is talking.\n- Each human should own a **relationship track + private memories**.\n- The large language model is the mouth. The pipeline before and after the model is the self.\n\nThe research instance is one character bound to one host and one primary relationship. The product is the same character engine with **accounts**, **isolated tracks**, and **no host lock-in**.\n\n## Read in this order\n\n1. [docs/00-strategy.md](docs/00-strategy.md) — docs vs FOSSIL vs knowledge graph", "truncated": false, "loaded": [], "display": {"type": "file", "path": "D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-product\\.kilo\\worktrees\\separate-binder\\README.md", "text": "# Hades Product\n\nThis repository is the **product specification and architecture home** for Hades.\n\nIt is not the live research instance. The living engine and state live in the runtime / memories trees. This repo exists so product work has a durable, anonymized map of *how she works* and *what must change* to ship a host-independent, multi-user Hades.\n\n## What Hades is\n\nHades is a **persistent character runtime**, not a chatbot wrapper.\n\n- Personality is a shared substrate (soul + locks + few-shots).\n- Mood, fatigue, circadian rhythm, and idle inner life keep moving when nobody is talking.\n- Each human should own a **relationship track + private memories**.\n- The large language model is the mouth. The pipeline before and after the model is the self.\n\nThe research instance is one character bound to one host and one primary relationship. The product is the same character engine with **accounts**, **isolated tracks**, and **no host lock-in**.\n\n## Read in this order\n\n1. [docs/00-strategy.md](docs/00-strategy.md) — docs vs FOSSIL vs knowledge graph\n2. [docs/01-how-she-works.md](docs/01-how-she-works.md) — turn loop and idle life\n3. [docs/02-identity-and-relationships.md](docs/02-identity-and-relationships.md) — who she thinks she is talking to\n4. [docs/03-memory-and-inner-life.md](docs/03-memory-and-inner-life.md) — what actually persists\n5. [docs/04-product-architecture.md](docs/04-product-architecture.md) — auth, API, tenancy\n6. [docs/05-workspace.md](docs/05-workspace.md) — local Cursor workspace for all three repos\n7. [docs/MODULE_GRAPH.yaml](docs/MODULE_GRAPH.yaml) — how files link\n8. [docs/PRIVACY.md](docs/PRIVACY.md) — no private names in this repo\n\n## Local workspace\n\nLong-term file inspection happens in Cursor, not in chat.\n\n- [hades.code-workspace](hades.code-workspace) — multi-root window over sibling clones\n- [tools/transcript_stats.py](tools/transcript_stats.py) — stream the gateway export; write counts only\n- [.cursor/rules/privacy.mdc](.cursor/rules/privacy.mdc) — keep names and raw chats out of this repo\n\n```bash\npython3 tools/transcript_stats.py --memories ../hades-v2-memories --out docs/transcripts-stats.md\n```\n\n## Source trees (research)\n\n| Repo | Role |\n|---|---|\n| Runtime repo | Code + contracts (`schema.yaml`, `dynamics.yaml`, engine) |\n| Memories repo | Live backup of state + a newer pipeline copy |\n| This repo | Product docs and eventual extracted runtime |\n\nDo not copy live secrets, passphrases, API keys, or private display names here.", "lineStart": 1, "lineEnd": 49, "totalLines": 49, "truncated": false}, "approval": {"source": "agent", "agent": "code", "rule": {"permission": "read", "pattern": "*", "action": "allow"}}}, "title": "README.md", "time": {"start": 1789773690929, "end": 1789773690970}}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6d33834001Y50lDEWCdDiVd8", "message_id": "msg_0b6d3227d00145s7uK4IPxUf7T", "time_created": 1789773690932, "time_updated": 1789773691332, "data": {"type": "tool", "tool": "read", "callID": "call-5838f3f7-9751-4ce4-bb7e-5a610e9841b7-32", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"filePath": "D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-product\\.kilo\\worktrees\\separate-binder\\docs\\05-workspace.md"}, "output": "<path>D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-product\\.kilo\\worktrees\\separate-binder\\docs\\05-workspace.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Long-term workspace\n2: \n3: This chat cannot be the repo browser. The durable setup is three sibling clones plus Cursor (or VS Code).\n4: \n5: ## Layout\n6: \n7: ```\n8: hades-workspace/\n9:   hades-v2/                 # runtime / engine\n10:   hades-v2-memories/        # live state backup + gateway transcript export\n11:   hades-product/            # this repo — anonymized spec only\n12:   hades.code-workspace      # copy from this repo, or open this file after adjusting paths\n13: ```\n14: \n15: Clone next to each other. Open `hades.code-workspace` so search hits all three roots.\n16: \n17: ```bash\n18: mkdir -p ~/hades-workspace && cd ~/hades-workspace\n19: git clone git@github.com:Pukujan/hades-v2.git\n20: git clone git@github.com:Pukujan/hades-v2-memories.git\n21: git clone git@github.com:Pukujan/hades-product.git\n22: cp hades-product/hades.code-workspace .\n23: ```\n24: \n25: Edit the workspace file if your folder names differ.\n26: \n27: ## Who does what\n28: \n29: | Place | Job |\n30: |---|---|\n31: | Cursor / local | Read every file, stream large JSONL, edit code, run tools |\n32: | This product repo | Architecture, contracts, anonymized stats |\n33: | Grok chat with GitHub | Review small derived files, write docs |\n34: | Live host / bot | After the runtime is extracted — not for archaeology |\n35: \n36: ## Rules\n37: \n38: See [PRIVACY.md](PRIVACY.md).\n39: \n40: - Never copy raw transcript shards into this repo.\n41: - Never commit private first names, tokens, passphrases, or numeric chat IDs here.\n42: - Stats and schema only. If you need example voice lines, redact them first.\n43: \n44: ## First hour\n45: \n46: 1. Open the multi-root workspace.\n47: 2. Confirm Cursor/VS Code can search `hades-v2-memories/hades-v2/conversations/`.\n48: 3. From `hades-product`:\n49: \n50: ```bash\n51: python tools/transcript_stats.py \\\n52:   --memories ../hades-v2-memories \\\n53:   --out docs/transcripts-stats.md\n54: ```\n55: \n56: 4. Commit only the stats markdown, not the JSONL.\n57: 5. Bring `docs/transcripts-stats.md` back to the product-doc thread if you want the spec updated from real counts.\n58: \n59: ## What the memories export is\n60: \n61: `hades-v2-memories/hades-v2/conversations/` is a Hermes gateway dump:\n62: \n63: - `sessions.jsonl` — session metadata\n64: - `messages-0001.jsonl` … `messages-0010.jsonl` — turns (user / assistant / tool / reasoning)\n65: \n66: Most sessions are cron and subagent, not human chat. Treat Telegram/DM rows as the relationship mouth. Personality and relationship state still live in soul, locks, registers, and `relations.yaml` — not in this dump alone.\n67: \n68: ## Do not use as the inspection layer\n69: \n70: - FOSSIL packs (research appendix only)\n71: - The in-world property graph (her fiction, not the codebase)\n72: - Uploading 47MB shards into a chat\n\n(End of file - total 72 lines)\n</content>", "metadata": {"preview": "# Long-term workspace\n\nThis chat cannot be the repo browser. The durable setup is three sibling clones plus Cursor (or VS Code).\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nhades-workspace/\n  hades-v2/                 # runtime / engine\n  hades-v2-memories/        # live state backup + gateway transcript export\n  hades-product/            # this repo — anonymized spec only\n  hades.code-workspace      # copy from this repo, or open this file after adjusting paths\n```\n\nClone next to each other. Open `hades.code-workspace` so search hits all three roots.\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/hades-workspace && cd ~/hades-workspace\ngit clone git@github.com:Pukujan/hades-v2.git\ngit clone git@github.com:Pukujan/hades-v2-memories.git", "truncated": false, "loaded": [], "display": {"type": "file", "path": "D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-product\\.kilo\\worktrees\\separate-binder\\docs\\05-workspace.md", "text": "# Long-term workspace\n\nThis chat cannot be the repo browser. The durable setup is three sibling clones plus Cursor (or VS Code).\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nhades-workspace/\n  hades-v2/                 # runtime / engine\n  hades-v2-memories/        # live state backup + gateway transcript export\n  hades-product/            # this repo — anonymized spec only\n  hades.code-workspace      # copy from this repo, or open this file after adjusting paths\n```\n\nClone next to each other. Open `hades.code-workspace` so search h