: "completed", "input": {"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.16634", "timeout": 20}, "output": " \\[2303.16634\\] G-Eval: NLG Evaluation using GPT-4 with Better Human Alignment                               \n\n[Skip to main content](#content)\n\n[](https://arxiv.org/IgnoreMe)[![archive](/static/base/1.0.1/images/arxiv-logo-primary-light.svg)](https://arxiv.org/)\n\n[Search](https://arxiv.org/search) [Submit](https://arxiv.org/user/create) [Donate](https://info.arxiv.org/about/donate.html) [Log in](https://arxiv.org/login)\n\nSearch arXiv   \n\nPress Enter to search · [Advanced search](https://arxiv.org/search/advanced)\n\n# Computer Science > Computation and Language\n\n**arXiv:2303.16634** (cs)\n\n\\[Submitted on 29 Mar 2023 ([v1](https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.16634v1)), last revised 23 May 2023 (this version, v3)\\]\n\n# Title:G-Eval: NLG Evaluation using GPT-4 with Better Human Alignment\n\nAuthors:[Yang Liu](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Liu,+Y), [Dan Iter](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Iter,+D), [Yichong Xu](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Xu,+Y), [Shuohang Wang](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Wang,+S), [Ruochen Xu](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Xu,+R), [Chenguang Zhu](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Zhu,+C)\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled G-Eval: NLG Evaluation using GPT-4 with Better Human Alignment, by Yang Liu and 4 other authors\n\n[View PDF](/pdf/2303.16634) [HTML (experimental)](https://arxiv.org/html/2303.16634v3)\n\n> Abstract:The quality of texts generated by natural language generation (NLG) systems is hard to measure automatically. Conventional reference-based metrics, such as BLEU and ROUGE, have been shown to have relatively low correlation with human judgments, especially for tasks that require creativity and diversity. Recent studies suggest using large language models (LLMs) as reference-free metrics for NLG evaluation, which have the benefit of being applicable to new tasks that lack human references. However, these LLM-based evaluators still have lower human correspondence than medium-size neural evaluators. In this work, we present G-Eval, a framework of using large language models with chain-of-thoughts (CoT) and a form-filling paradigm, to assess the quality of NLG outputs. We experiment with two generation tasks, text summarization and dialogue generation. We show that G-Eval with GPT-4 as the backbone model achieves a Spearman correlation of 0.514 with human on summarization task, outperforming all previous methods by a large margin. We also propose preliminary analysis on the behavior of LLM-based evaluators, and highlight the potential issue of LLM-based evaluators having a bias towards the LLM-generated texts. The code is at [this https URL](https://github.com/nlpyang/geval)\n\nSubjects:\n\nComputation and Language (cs.CL); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\n\nCite as:\n\n[arXiv:2303.16634](https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.16634) \\[cs.CL\\]\n\n \n\n(or [arXiv:2303.16634v3](https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.16634v3) \\[cs.CL\\] for this version)\n\n \n\n[https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2303.16634](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2303.16634)\n\nFocus to learn more\n\narXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\n\n## Submission history\n\nFrom: Yang Liu \\[[view email](/show-email/9756619f/2303.16634)\\]  \n**[\\[v1\\]](/abs/2303.16634v1)** Wed, 29 Mar 2023 12:46:54 UTC (242 KB)  \n**[\\[v2\\]](/abs/2303.16634v2)** Thu, 6 Apr 2023 23:49:08 UTC (209 KB)  \n**\\[v3\\]** Tue, 23 May 2023 22:12:16 UTC (209 KB)  \n\nFull-text links:\n\n## Access Paper:\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled G-Eval: NLG Evaluation using GPT-4 with Better Human Alignment, by Yang Liu and 4 other authors\n\n-   [View PDF](/pdf/2303.16634)\n-   [HTML (experimental)](https://arxiv.org/html/2303.16634v3)\n-   [TeX Source](/src/2303.16634)\n\n [![license icon](https://arxiv.org/icons/licenses/by-nc-nd-4.0.png) view license](http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ \"Rights to this article\")\n\n### Current browse context:\n\ncs.CL\n\n[< prev](/prevnext?id=2303.16634&function=prev&context=cs.CL \"previous in cs.CL (accesskey p)\")   |   [next >](/prevnext?id=2303.16634&function=next&context=cs.CL \"next in cs.CL (accesskey n)\")  \n\n[new](/list/cs.CL/new) | [recent](/list/cs.CL/recent) | [2023-03](/list/cs.CL/2023-03)\n\nChange to browse by:\n\n[cs](/abs/2303.16634?context=cs)  \n[cs.AI](/abs/2303.16634?context=cs.AI)  \n\n### References & Citations\n\n-   [NASA ADS](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/arXiv:2303.16634)\n-   [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?arxiv_id=2303.16634)\n-   [Semantic Scholar](https://api.semanticscholar.org/arXiv:2303.16634)\n\n### [3 blog links](/tb/2303.16634)\n\n([what is this?](https://info.arxiv.org/help/trackback.html))\n\nexport BibTeX citation Loading...\n\n## BibTeX formatted citation\n\n×\n\nloading...\n\nData provided by:\n\n### Bookmark\n\n [![BibSonomy](/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/social/bibsonomy.png)](http://www.bibsonomy.org/BibtexHandler?requTask=upload&url=https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.16634&description=G-Eval: NLG Evaluation using GPT-4 with Better Human Alignment \"Bookmark on BibSonomy\")[![Reddit](/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/social/reddit.png)](https://reddit.com/submit?url=https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.16634&title=G-Eval: NLG Evaluation using GPT-4 with Better Human Alignment \"Bookmark on Reddit\")\n\n Bibliographic Tools\n\n# Bibliographic and Citation Tools\n\n Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\n\nBibliographic Explorer *([What is the Explorer?](https://info.arxiv.org/labs/showcase.html#arxiv-bibliographic-explorer))*\n\n Connected Papers Toggle\n\nConnected Papers *([What is Connected Papers?](https://www.connectedpapers.com/about))*\n\n Litmaps Toggle\n\nLitmaps *([What is Litmaps?](https://www.litmaps.co/))*\n\n scite.ai Toggle\n\nscite Smart Citations *([What are Smart Citations?](https://www.scite.ai/))*\n\n