ate-binder\\docs\\03-memory-and-inner-life.md", "limit": 80}, "output": "<path>D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-product\\.kilo\\worktrees\\separate-binder\\docs\\03-memory-and-inner-life.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Memory and inner life\n2: \n3: What actually persists. The chat UI is not the store. Cron is not a user.\n4: \n5: Shared character substrate (soul, locks, circadian, mood engines) is one. Relationship memories are per `person_id`. Product must not mix tracks.\n6: \n7: ## Layers\n8: \n9: ```text\n10: working memory (now)\n11:   -> episodic (experiences, slower recall)\n12:   -> semantic (consolidated patterns)\n13: idle: thoughts.jsonl, dreams, daily-life packet\n14: forgetting: archive by salience, do not hard-delete\n15: ```\n16: \n17: | Layer | Job | Product rule |\n18: |---|---|---|\n19: | Working | Last thoughts, live mood, current activity, recent turns | Injected every turn. Short TTL. |\n20: | Episodic | Experiences with emotional weight | Per `person_id` when the memory is about a human |\n21: | Semantic | Patterns after consolidation | Shared skills/world vs per-track people-facts must be split |\n22: | Thought log | Idle inner monologue (~10 min) | Not user-visible unless a later proactive rule fires |\n23: | Dreams | 0–4am, fragmented, short TTL | Inner. Do not narrate to the user as a morning recap by default |\n24: | Daily life | Where she is in her own world | Satellite packet around soul. Fiction, not the human’s calendar |\n25: | Virtual friends | Simulated cast | `virtual_friend`. Never an account |\n26: | mem0 / profile MEMORY | External memory provider + profile files | Research dump. Product: structured per-track store, no raw USER.md |\n27: \n28: Primary-track memories decay slower than stranger tracks. Emotional intensity resists forgetting. Frequency of recall resists forgetting. Archive ≠ delete.\n29: \n30: ## Idle loop (cron)\n31: \n32: Every ~10 minutes, a separate process:\n33: \n34: 1. Read mood, relations, silence\n35: 2. Tick existential state\n36: 3. Daily-life orchestrator (rhythm, reading, virtual friends, empathy, ontology)\n37: 4. Pick a thought category\n38: 5. Write a short inner thought\n39: 6. Maybe promote high-weight thoughts to episodic\n40: 7. Small mood writeback\n41: 8. Rarely consider a proactive outbound message\n42: \n43: It must not block the live turn. Gateway `source=cron` sessions are this loop (or Hermes wrapping it), not Telegram DMs.\n44: \n45: Observed export: 512 cron sessions, almost all `cron_complete`, median ~13 messages, models mostly `aux` / `deepseek-v4-flash`. Sampled recent cron turns are tool-heavy inner work with almost no `[IMG:]`. Do not mine cron for partner-mouth voice.\n46: \n47: Proactive pings are specified as rare and emotionally significant. Product default: **off** until an account setting allows them.\n48: \n49: ## What is shared vs per-user\n50: \n51: | Shared (character) | Per `person_id` (track) |\n52: |---|---|\n53: | Soul, few-shots, anti-assistant | Register, attachment, last contact |\n54: | Circadian wave, fatigue model | Conversation recall, private episodic |\n55: | Image library / matcher | Secrets the other tracks must not see |\n56: | Idle daily-life fiction | Partner-track vs sister-track facts |\n57: \n58: `sister` never receives partner-track memories. `stranger` gets no private track. `virtual_friend` is not a tenant.\n59: \n60: ## Research debt (do not ship)\n61: \n62: - Hardcoded name maps for recall weights and registers\n63: - Profile `USER.md` / `MEMORY.md` as the source of truth\n64: - One global marriage/secrets file\n65: - Host paths, live API keys, object-store account IDs\n66: \n67: Product identity is flags on `person_id`. Product memory is a store keyed by `account_id` + `person_id`.\n\n(End of file - total 67 lines)\n</content>", "metadata": {"preview": "# Memory and inner life\n\nWhat actually persists. The chat UI is not the store. Cron is not a user.\n\nShared character substrate (soul, locks, circadian, mood engines) is one. Relationship memories are per `person_id`. Product must not mix tracks.\n\n## Layers\n\n```text\nworking memory (now)\n  -> episodic (experiences, slower recall)\n  -> semantic (consolidated patterns)\nidle: thoughts.jsonl, dreams, daily-life packet\nforgetting: archive by salience, do not hard-delete\n```\n\n| Layer | Job | Product rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| Working | Last thoughts, live mood, current activity, recent turns | Injected every turn. Short TTL. |\n| Episodic | Experiences with emotional weight | Per `person_id` when the memory is about a human |", "truncated": false, "loaded": [], "display": {"type": "file", "path": "D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-product\\.kilo\\worktrees\\separate-binder\\docs\\03-memory-and-inner-life.md", "text": "# Memory and inner life\n\nWhat actually persists. The chat UI is not the store. Cron is not a user.\n\nShared character substrate (soul, locks, circadian, mood engines) is one. Relationship memories are per `person_id`. Product must not mix tracks.\n\n## Layers\n\n```text\nworking memory (now)\n  -> episodic (experiences, slower recall)\n  -> semantic (consolidated patterns)\nidle: thoughts.jsonl, dreams, daily-life packet\nforgetting: archive by salience, do not hard-delete\n```\n\n| Layer | Job | Product rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| Working | Last thoughts, live mood, current activity, recent turns | Injected every turn. Short TTL. |\n| Episodic | Experiences with emotional weight | Per `person_id` when the memory is about a human |\n| Semantic | Patterns after consolidation | Shared skills/world vs per-track people-facts must be split |\n| Thought log | Idle inner monologue (~10 min) | Not user-visible unless a later proactive rule fires |\n| Dreams | 0–4am, fragmented, short TTL | Inner. Do not narrate to the user as a morning recap by default |\n| Daily life | Where she is in her own world | Satellite packet around soul. Fiction, not the human’s calendar |\n| Virtual friends | Simulated cast | `virtual_friend`. Never an account |\n| mem0 / profile MEMORY | External memory provider + profile files | Research dump. Product: structured per-track store, no raw USER.md |\n\nPrimary-track memories decay slower than stranger tracks. Emotional intensity resists forgetting. Frequency of recall resists forgetting. Archive ≠ delete.\n\n## Idle loop (cron)\n\nEvery ~10 minutes, a separate process:\n\n1. Read mood, relations, silence\n2. Tick existential state\n3. Daily-life orchestrator (rhythm, reading, virtual friends, empathy, ontology)\n4. Pick a thought category\n5. Write a short inner thought\n6. Maybe promote high-weight thoughts to episodic\n7. Small mood writeback\n8. Rarely consider a proactive outbound message\n\nIt must not block the live turn. Gateway `source=cron` sessions are this loop (or Hermes wrapping it), not Telegram DMs.\n\nObserved export: 512 cron sessions, almost all `cron_complete`, median ~13 messages, models mostly `aux` / `deepseek-v4-flash`. Sampled recent cron turns are tool-heavy inner work with almost no `[IMG:]`. Do not mine cron for partner-mouth voice.\n\nProactive pings are specified as rare and emotionally significant. Product default: **off** until an account setting allows them.\n\n## What is shared vs per-user\n\n| Shared (character) | Per `person_id` (track) |\n|---|---|\n| Soul, few-shots, anti-assistant | Register, attachment, last contact |\n| Circadian wave, fatigue model | Conversation recall, private episodic |\n| Image library / matcher | Secrets the other tracks must not see |\n| Idle daily-life fiction | Partner-track vs sister-track facts |\n\n`sister` never receives partner-track memories. `stranger` gets no private track. `virtual_friend` is not a tenant.\n\n## Research debt (do not ship)\n\n- Hardcoded name maps for recall weights and registers\n- Profile `USER.md` / `MEMORY.md` as the source of truth\n- One global marriage/secrets file\n- Host paths, live API keys, object-store account IDs\n\nProduct identity is flags on `person_id`. Product memory is a store keyed by `account_id` + `person_id`.", "lineStart": 1, "lineEnd": 67, "totalLines": 67, "truncated": false}, "approval": {"source": "agent", "agent": "ask", "rule": {"permission": "read", "pattern": "*", "action": "allow"}}}, "title": "docs\\03-memory-and-inner-life.md", "time": {"start": 1789774400857, "end": 1789774400914}}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6de0d5d0019bsDr2SV0NVGyl", "message_id": "msg_0b6ddface0015JnYApWmgvxW1a", "time_created": 1789774400862, "time_updated": 1789774401674, "data": {"type": "tool", "tool": "grep", "callID": "call-5f833901-02c3-4af2-b8b9-6fc3b18c8916-99", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"pattern": "mood_snapshot|pre-llm|pre_llm|tier_state", "path": "D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-v2-memories\\hades-v2", "include": "*.{py,md,json}", "limit": 40}, "output": "Found 40 matches (more matches available)\nD:\\claude\\hades\\hades-v2-memories\\hades-v2\\MANIFEST.md:\n  Line 38: │       │   └── pre-llm-pipeline/       # Pre-LLM pipeline plugin\r\n\n  Line 96: │       │   └── pre-llm-pipeline/\r\n\n  Line 170: In `pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py`:\r\n\n  Line 299: The pre-llm-pipeline plugin MUST resolve ALL paths through the three\r\n\n  Line 331: - `pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py` — canonical path variables, no fallbacks\r\n\n  Line 332: - `pre-llm-pipeline/image_matcher.py` — hardcoded paths removed\r\n\n  Line 333: - `pre-llm-pipeline/test_*.py` and `rebuild_embeddings*.py` — path references fixed\r\n\n\nD:\\claude\\hades\\hades-v2-memories\\hades-v2\\docs\\hades-personality-design.md:\n  Line 1218: plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/\r\n\n  Line 2210: # In the pre_llm_call hook function, add:\r\n\n  Line 2217: # Inside the pre_llm_call hook, after computing emotion engine state:\r\n\n\nD:\\claude\\hades\\hades-v2-memories\\hades-v2\\profile\\soul.md:\n  Line 3: ## Pre-response ritual (DISABLED — moved to pre-llm plugin)\r\n\n  Line 5: The pre_response.py functionality (FAISS image cadence + delivery) is being migrated to the pre-llm-pipeline Hermes plugin, which runs before every LLM call.\r\n\n  Line 7: The soul.md identity rules (personality lock, I/T/D scaling) are now enforced by the pre-llm-pipeline plugin at the system prompt level.\r\n\n\nD:\\claude\\hades\\hades-v2-memories\\hades-v2\\docs\\hades-v2-clone-strategy.md:\n  Line 34: │   └── pre-llm-pipeline/       # 1879-line God Object plugin\r\n\n  Line 56: │   │   ├── tier_state.json\r\n\n  Line 155: #### 2d. `pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py` — Hardcoded Paths (CRITICAL)\r\n\n  Line 183: **Files in `pre-llm-pipeline/` with hardcoded paths that need updating for v2:**\r\n\n  Line 295: **And in the v2 plugin:** `pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py:103`:\r\n\n  Line 315: - `tier_state.json` — 4-tier state machine\r\n\n  Line 332: - `tier_state.json`\r\n\n  Line 405: | **Tier state JSON** | `data/tier_state.json` (host + engine) | `emotion-project-host-v2/data/tier_state.json` | ✅ Auto-isolated |\r\n\n  Line 474: - Run `python -c \"from pre_llm_pipeline import _run_pipeline; print(_run_pipeline())\"` in v2 plugin\r\n\n  Line 680: # In hades/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py:103\r\n\n  Line 752: 2. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py:103` — `DAEMON_PORT = 19273` → `19274`\r\n\n  Line 753: 3. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/scene_analysis.py:45` — hardcoded data path\r\n\n  Line 754: 4. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/image_matcher.py` — 8 hardcoded paths (lines 65, 70, 75, 505, 2206, 2216, 2226, 2657)\r\n\n  Line 755: 5. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/retag_v2.py:21` — hardcoded `.env` path\r\n\n  Line 756: 6. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/test_*.py` — multiple test files with hardcoded paths\r\n\n  Line 757: 7. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/rebuild_embeddings*.py` — hardcoded paths\r\n\n  Line 758: 8. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/vision_reindex*.py` — hardcoded paths\r\n\n  Line 778: 25. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py:88` — covered by `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_HOST`\r\n\n  Line 779: 26. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py:89` — covered by `HADES_EMOTION_PROJECT_ROOT`\r\n\n  Line 780: 27. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py:95` — covered by `HERMES_HOME`\r\n\n  Line 787: 31. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py:117` — shared venv path (read-only)\r\n\n  Line 788: 32. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py:104` — `DAEMON_SCRIPT` resolves via `FAISS_SCRIPTS_DIR` (relative)\r\n\n  Line 789: 33. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py:105` — `DAEMON_PID_FILE` resolves via `HERMES_ROOT` (env var)\r\n\n  Line 793: 37. `hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/plugin.yaml` — no paths\r\n\n  Line 815: # (Edit hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/__init__.py:103)\r\n\n  Line 852: find /d/hermes/profiles/hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/ -name \"*.py\" -exec sed -i \\\r\n\n  Line 854: find /d/hermes/profiles/hades-v2/plugins/pre-llm-pipeline/ -name \"*.py\" -exec sed -i \\\r\n\n\n40 matches limit reached. Use limit=80 for more, or refine pattern.", "metadata": {"matches": 40, "truncated": true, "approval": {"source": "manual", "outsideWorkspace": true, "outsideWorkspacePath": "D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-v2-memories\\hades-v2"}}, "title": "mood_snapshot|pre-llm|pre_llm|tier_state", "time": {"start": 1789774401165, "end": 1789774401673}}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6de0e90001fxd7zXZHAXEdor", "message_id": "msg_0b6ddface0015JnYApWmgvxW1a", "time_created": 1789774401168, "time_updated": 1789774401533, "data": {"type": "tool", "tool": "glob", "callID": "call-5f833901-02c3-4af2-b8b9-6fc3b18c8916-100", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"pattern": "**/.git", "path": "D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-v2-memories"}, "output": "No files found", "metadata": {"count": 0, "truncated": false, "approval": {"source": "manual", "outsideWorkspace": true, "outsideWorkspacePath": "D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-v2-memories"}}, "title": "..\\..\\..\\..\\hades-v2-memories", "time": {"start": 1789774401232, "end": 1789774401532}}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6de121c001