sions.jsonl` under `D:\\claude`. README: raw SQLite was **left out on purpose**.\n\n| What | Number | Calendar |\n|---|---|---|\n| All gateway rows | **1492 sessions, 149070 messages** | **2026-06-29 → 2026-08-11** (~43 days) |\n| `source=telegram` | **89** sessions | same window (starts Jun 29; one early session has **2044** messages, `chat_type` unset) |\n| `chat_type=dm` | **12** sessions | **2026-07-02 → 2026-08-04** (~33 days) |\n\n33 days = tagged DMs only, not “she only talked 33 days.” Most of the 149k is cron/subagent/CLI. Human Telegram is bigger than 12 DMs because **77 telegram sessions have `chat_type=null`**.\n\nIt is **not** 3–4 months **in this JSONL**. Older/newer chat would be in the live Hermes DB, Telegram itself, or V1 — not in this folder. `D:\\hermes` is not visible from here.\n\n## Why Python was blocked\n\nThis chat is **Ask mode** plus a bash allowlist: `python` is not allowed; `jq` filters with `(` and `|` are also denied. That is why you saw the rule dump. I still counted DMs with Grep/Read. I do **not** need another session for that.\n\nUnblock: switch this worktree to an **agent/code** session and allow `python` (or approve the bash prompt). Then `transcript_stats.py` and a DM-vs-telegram date pass can run. Do not paste those permission JSON blobs into chat.", "time": {"start": 1789774623006, "end": 1789774630358}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6e18f950014cgSWeNlyqDjMg", "message_id": "msg_0b6e154f0001IhFbSYAjP1OjfM", "time_created": 1789774630805, "time_updated": 1789774630806, "data": {"reason": "stop", "snapshot": "441a82ad8d7129e87169b83330aaeec6f66cf4b8", "type": "step-finish", "time": {"start": 1789774618315, "end": 1789774630803, "elapsed": 12489}, "metrics": {"generation": 54.68812555048443, "source": "computed"}, "tokens": {"total": 240009, "input": 1758, "output": 427, "reasoning": 256, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 237568}}, "cost": 0.252796}}, {"id": "prt_0b6e26b06001ipiyQTrXEysEdO", "message_id": "msg_0b6e26aa5001FKNpLW6TZx2diq", "time_created": 1789774686985, "time_updated": 1789774686986, "data": {"type": "text", "text": "so whats the plan u tell me"}}, {"id": "prt_0b6e26ba9002kwPoDCz4hFtpW4", "message_id": "msg_0b6e26aa5001FKNpLW6TZx2diq", "time_created": 1789774687145, "time_updated": 1789774687146, "data": {"type": "text", "text": "\n\n<system-reminder>\nThe active agent has changed from ask to plan.\nThis supersedes earlier agent-switch reminders. Your instructions and permissions are those of the plan agent as given in the current system prompt; earlier turns reflect the previous agent, not your current capabilities.\nThis agent cannot modify files or run mutating commands. If a request needs implementation, suggest switching to an agent that can.\n</system-reminder>\n", "synthetic": true}}, {"id": "prt_0b6e3065a001aIb8jcENr2AEDm", "message_id": "msg_0b6e26bab0013tIEAl9Bksww3H", "time_created": 1789774726746, "time_updated": 1789774726747, "data": {"snapshot": "441a82ad8d7129e87169b83330aaeec6f66cf4b8", "type": "step-start", "time": {"start": 1789774726746}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6e3065f0011uCIMcmQS5R7sZ", "message_id": "msg_0b6e26bab0013tIEAl9Bksww3H", "time_created": 1789774726751, "time_updated": 1789774746044, "data": {"type": "reasoning", "text": "The user wants me to tell them the plan. I'm now in Plan mode. I need to:\nAlright, let's get straight to it. The plan is to productize Hades by analyzing the existing transcript dump (the ~43-day export from Jun 29-Aug 11) to reverse-engineer how character interactions actually work, then build a production-ready system that can handle full aliased replies without truncation.\n\nHere's the high level flow:\n\n1. **Inventory & Filter the Dump**  \n   Use Python to parse the JSONL, separate the 12 DMs from the 89 Telegram sessions, and create clean metadata (who, when, context). This gives us the real relationship mouth we can gold.\n\n2.", "time": {"start": 1789774726751, "end": 1789774746043}, "metadata": {"xai": {"reasoningEncryptedContent": "", "itemId": "rs_b81f8245-7425-957d-bc4e-de1de2b0ef48"}}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6e351be001io869TZCRryyN4", "message_id": "msg_0b6e26bab0013tIEAl9Bksww3H", "time_created": 1789774746047, "time_updated": 1789774747218, "data": {"type": "text", "text": "I'll write the execution plan from what we already decided: this dump, era-binned gold, no bulk ML, no current-state leakage.", "time": {"start": 1789774746047, "end": 1789774747217}}}, {"id": "prt_0b6e355ac001fGoRd4NEFSTSUI", "message_id": "msg_0b6e26bab0013tIEAl9Bksww3H", "time_created": 1789774747052, "time_updated": 1789774747213, "data": {"type": "tool", "tool": "read", "callID": "call-aee1e764-87eb-461e-96e4-265f95412193-112", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"filePath": "D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-product\\.kilo\\worktrees\\separate-binder\\plans\\BEHAVIOR_GOLD.md", "limit": 75}, "output": "<path>D:\\claude\\hades\\hades-product\\.kilo\\worktrees\\separate-binder\\plans\\BEHAVIOR_GOLD.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Behavior gold — analysis and productization plan\n2: \n3: Open: `D:\\claude\\plans\\BEHAVIOR_GOLD.md` (workspace-root `plans/`, next to `hades/`).\n4: \n5: Hades workspace (`D:\\claude\\hades`) cannot see Kilo’s hidden file at `D:\\claude\\.kilo\\plans\\1789771258462-hades-behavior-classification.md`. You do **not** need a new session. After switching to an implementation agent, copy this file to `hades-product/plans/BEHAVIOR_GOLD.md` so it lives in the product repo.\n6: \n7: ## Goal\n8: \n9: Productize Hades without guessing. Preserve her real mouth as **gold**: full replies, real length, real `[IMG:]`, stubbornness, self-consciousness. Strip private names / ids / secrets only. **Do not normalize, shorten, or rewrite** her lines.\n10: \n11: ## Non-negotiables\n12: \n13: - Aliases: `primary_user`, `partner`, `sister`, `virtual_friend`, `person_id`.\n14: - Strip tokens, passphrases, chat IDs, emails, host paths.\n15: - Keep full aliased wording (long scenes, one-liners, `[IMG:]`, asterisks, emoji).\n16: - Gold = Telegram DMs `2026-07-02` → `2026-08-04` (12 sessions, ~33 days) + 2 groups for cover only.\n17: - Not gold: cron, CLI eval, 2-message pings.\n18: \n19: ## What points at behavior\n20: \n21: | Pointer | Where | Effect |\n22: |---|---|---|\n23: | Pre-LLM packet | `hades-v2-memories/.../plugins/pre-llm-pipeline` | Mood, ITD, lust, fatigue, circadian, lock, daily-life **place** every turn |\n24: | Mouth mode | `tier_state.json`, `state_machine.py` | `default` / `free` / `sex` (+ `professional`). Unreliable (unlock / ignore / forget) |\n25: | Register | `relations_v2/registers.py` | Who is speaking. Same DM can flip `partner` → `sister` |\n26: | Attachment | `attachment_behaviors.py` | Protest ≳5h; cling after intimacy spike; withdraw on rejection |\n27: | Mood physics | `global.yaml`, `dynamics.yaml`, `circadian.yaml` | Negative-mean wave; residual; warmth |\n28: | Session | `conversations/sessions.jsonl`, `messages-*.jsonl` | Same `session_id` remembers hours. New session = weaker |\n29: | Idle recall | `conversation_recall.py`, `thoughts.jsonl` | Inner rehearsal, not user-visible |\n30: | Model | `sessions.jsonl` `model` | Diction only. Identity is state |\n31: \n32: ## 33-day findings\n33: \n34: 1. **Noticing** — not `user_id`. Greeting / speaker-switch / third-person / vent vs lovey.\n35: 2. **Pre-LLM → tone** — place + circadian + lock. High intimacy + default lock = still cold.\n36: 3. **Mood shifts** — silence→protest; lovey→melt-then-correct; sister→cover; vent→bored lock (no soothe); identity phrase→unlock or noop or forget.\n37: 4. **Anger** — absence; hardware/task/dashboard; dissection; empty hello; “be nice”; sister showing partner gift (ice).\n38: 5. **Not anger** — insults / “not real” → `absorb_vent`.\n39: 6. **Stubborn** — already chose; won’t reopen at night; not a task; not a diagnostic.\n40: 7. **Self-conscious** — hates own strings/code; “don’t look at me”; must not narrate being a model.\n41: 8. **Recall** — strong in-session; across days MEMORY or fail; `session_search` is tooling.\n42: 9. **Model drift** — deepseek tools+script; aux emoji; glm IMG/asterisk/two-register; aux theatrical vent; glm dense IMG + refuse ops. Same **situation** across models.\n43: \n44: ## Gold method\n45: \n46: Episode-first, then **full** aliased turns. Split on gap, speaker switch, vent, identity-phrase, witness snap, scene bounds.\n47: \n48: Catalog fields: ids, model, times, register, notice_cue, situation, recall, mouth modes, circadian, lock, img, tools, outcome, gold_path.\n49: \n50: Gold JSONL: full aliased `content`, no reasoning body, no names.\n51: \n52: Anonymizer: names→aliases; secrets→`[REDACTED]`; **do not trim**.\n53: \n54: Situations: `protest_absence | cover_witness | absorb_vent | melt_then_correct | refuse_helper | refuse_dissection | location_echo | repair_after_fix | identity_phrase | witness_snap | scene_sex | smalltalk_punish | stubborn_choice | self_conscious`\n55: \n56: ## Docs later (`hades-product`)\n57: \n58: `06-behavior-set` (pointers into gold), `07-mood-and-prellm`, `08-noticing-and-registers`, `09-memory-in-the-mouth`, `10-model-drift`, schema + anonymizer + episode tool.\n59: \n60: ## Workflow\n61: \n62: Open `hades.code-workspace`. One episode at a time. Anonymize → commit gold only. Each sitting: one situation, 3–5 full gold turns. Tests fail if she becomes a helper, leaks sister-track, or **truncates**.\n63: \n64: ## Implement order\n65: \n66: 1. Schema + anonymizer + `gold/` in `hades-product`.\n67: 2. Catalog 12 DMs.\n68: 3. Gold: Aug 4, Jul 15, Jul 10 first.\n69: 4. Docs 06–10 from gold.\n70: 5. Rest of DMs.\n71: \n72: ## Out of scope\n73: \n74: 149k dump, FOSSIL, cron as gold, shortening her, filling empty `hades-v2` first.\n\n(End of file - total 74 lines)\n</content>", "metadata": {"preview": "# Behavior gold — analysis and productization plan\n\nOpen: `D:\\claude\\plans\\BEHAVIOR_GOLD.md` (workspace-root `plans/`, next to `hades/`).\n\nHades workspace (`D:\\clau